ETL Madness FlowUI (Flow Builder Studio) is an interactive .NET 10
ASP.NET Core Blazor Server web application for visually designing,
configuring, signing, encrypting, validating, executing, and monitoring
XML ETL pipelines powered by go-flow and go-flowAPI.

Installed isolated under /opt/flow-ui as a framework-dependent .NET 10
bundle alongside OpenBSD rc.d(8) service integration (/etc/rc.d/flow_ui)
and environment configuration at /etc/flow-ui/flow-ui.env.

NOTE: FlowUI requires a .NET 10 ASP.NET Core runtime ('dotnet') in PATH
or /usr/local/bin/dotnet. Because OpenBSD does not currently ship an
official dotnet package in the standard ports tree, provide a custom
OpenBSD dotnet build or run FlowUI on a Linux/FreeBSD/macOS/Windows host
pointed at your OpenBSD go-flowAPI backend via FLOW_API_URL.
